<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>Refunds — Recruiter Lab</title></head><body><main><a class="back" href="/lucas-capability-os-pages/legal-recruiter-lab/">← Recruiter Lab</a><p class="kicker">PRE-LAUNCH POLICY</p><h1>Refunds</h1><p class="lead">Digital products should match what was promised and remain accessible after purchase.</p><section><h2>When to contact us</h2><p>Contact support if you were charged more than once, received the wrong product, cannot access the purchased file after a successful live purchase, or believe the product was materially misdescribed at checkout.</p></section><section><h2>Requests</h2><p>Refund requests will be reviewed against the purchase record, product description, delivery status, and applicable consumer law. Nothing in this policy limits rights that cannot legally be waived in the buyer’s jurisdiction.</p></section><section><h2>Digital delivery</h2><p>Because this is a downloadable digital product, access and delivery records may be relevant when reviewing a request. Test Mode orders are not real charges and are not eligible for cash refunds.</p></section><section><h2>How refunds are processed</h2><p>Approved refunds are processed through the payment platform used for the purchase. Processing and bank-posting times may vary by payment method and financial institution.</p></section><p class="note">Last updated: 8 September 2026. Pre-launch operational policy; not legal advice.</p><footer><a href="./privacy">Privacy</a><a href="./terms">Terms</a><a href="./support">Support</a></footer><p class="flow">Flow note — This page defines the pre-launch refund handling boundary without overriding mandatory consumer protections.</p></main></body></html><style>:root{--ink:#111;--paper:#f5f3ed;--line:#cbc8bf;--muted:#69675f}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}main{max-width:920px;margin:auto;padding:42px 24px 70px}.back,footer a{color:inherit}.kicker{margin-top:70px;font:700 10px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted)}h1{font-size:clamp(64px,12vw,120px);letter-spacing:-.07em;line-height:.85;margin:18px 0 36px}.lead{font-size:22px;line-height:1.5;max-width:720px}section{padding:28px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}h2{font-size:24px;margin:0 0 10px}p{line-height:1.7}section p,.note{color:#55534d}.note{font-size:12px}footer{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-top:1px solid #111;padding-top:24px;margin-top:40px;font-size:12px}.flow{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}</style>